WEBVTT

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:43.937
Tokugawa!

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.063
Tokugawa-<i>kun</i>!

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:51.778
The fool took my Destruction to the stomach.

00:01:52.404 --> 00:01:54.322
All to protect one kid.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:58.243
This is what happens when
you sacrifice yourself!

00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:00.662
Bastard!

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.167
You're...

00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:10.088
...the worst!

00:02:22.684 --> 00:02:28.690
"The Guided Ones"

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:32.110
What do you think you're doing?

00:02:32.944 --> 00:02:36.531
You might not escape this
encounter unscathed.

00:02:36.781 --> 00:02:39.492
Really? Why don't you try it, then?

00:02:40.035 --> 00:02:41.536
Ryoma Echizen...

00:02:42.787 --> 00:02:45.331
Don't interfere.

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:47.667
Tokugawa-<i>san</i>.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.085
I asked you once if

00:02:49.586 --> 00:02:52.839
there was anyone you'd give
your own life to beat.

00:02:54.049 --> 00:02:57.677
The man I'd give my life to beat

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.138
is right here.

00:03:03.641 --> 00:03:04.476
Please.

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:07.937
The game will resume!

00:03:08.355 --> 00:03:10.565
Game, five games to three!

00:03:10.565 --> 00:03:11.649
Tokugawa leads!

00:03:11.649 --> 00:03:13.234
Starting at love-forty!

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:15.528
One more point.

00:03:16.321 --> 00:03:18.740
I just need one more point.

00:03:19.449 --> 00:03:20.617
This is reckless!

00:03:20.617 --> 00:03:23.703
It's all he can do just to stay on his feet.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:26.956
He said he'd die to beat him.

00:03:26.956 --> 00:03:27.957
But...

00:03:27.957 --> 00:03:29.584
Just watch him.

00:03:29.584 --> 00:03:32.337
That's all we can do.

00:03:35.674 --> 00:03:38.885
You should've stayed on the ground.

00:03:39.177 --> 00:03:40.762
I told you!

00:03:40.762 --> 00:03:43.848
I'll bet my life on this match!

00:03:44.641 --> 00:03:46.142
Very well!

00:03:50.814 --> 00:03:52.524
Fifteen-forty!

00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:53.983
Tokugawa-<i>kun</i>!

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:09.582
Weak!

00:04:12.836 --> 00:04:14.087
Thirty-forty!

00:04:14.671 --> 00:04:19.175
This is the power of a player
who fights at the world level.

00:04:19.175 --> 00:04:23.054
He doesn't even compare to
anything we've seen before.

00:04:31.354 --> 00:04:33.773
You'd die to beat me?

00:04:34.858 --> 00:04:36.317
Weak!

00:04:39.487 --> 00:04:40.405
Black Hole!

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:45.660
Forty all!

00:04:46.036 --> 00:04:47.078
He caught up!

00:04:47.454 --> 00:04:49.998
He's suffered a lot of damage.

00:04:57.005 --> 00:04:58.548
He can't take any more.

00:05:05.055 --> 00:05:08.058
Until you die once and experience hell,

00:05:08.058 --> 00:05:09.642
you'll never beat me!

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:19.986
Tokugawa!

00:05:22.197 --> 00:05:24.449
He struck the ball while unconscious?

00:05:27.118 --> 00:05:29.913
I'm through wasting time.

00:05:29.913 --> 00:05:33.667
Crumble and fall apart along with your life!

00:05:34.042 --> 00:05:35.085
Destruction!

00:05:36.753 --> 00:05:38.963
Don't, Echizen.

00:05:39.631 --> 00:05:41.424
If you help him,

00:05:41.424 --> 00:05:43.343
they'll kick you out of the camp.

00:05:43.927 --> 00:05:45.428
Remember Kabaji.

00:05:49.557 --> 00:05:52.185
Per the rules of the U-17 training camp,

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:57.482
Munehiro Kabaji is ordered to leave the camp
for interfering with a match in progress.

00:05:59.484 --> 00:06:00.694
That's fine by me.

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:02.487
Die!

00:06:34.352 --> 00:06:35.228
Hey.

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.278
I'll beat you.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.079
Per the rules,

00:06:53.538 --> 00:06:57.000
Ryoma Echizen-<i>kun </i>is ordered
to leave the training camp.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:00.587
Oh, really?

00:07:00.587 --> 00:07:01.755
Tokugawa-<i>kun</i>!

00:07:04.591 --> 00:07:05.967
Take care of Tokugawa-<i>san</i>.

00:07:09.387 --> 00:07:10.388
Echizen!

00:07:13.308 --> 00:07:15.477
Coach, this isn't right!

00:07:15.477 --> 00:07:18.146
Yeah, he didn't do anything wrong!

00:07:18.146 --> 00:07:19.147
I won't accept this!

00:07:19.647 --> 00:07:20.815
Quiet!

00:07:20.815 --> 00:07:23.443
He knew what he was doing.

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:25.070
B-But, Atobe-<i>san</i>...

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.196
That's enough!

00:07:31.326 --> 00:07:32.619
Fool...

00:07:34.162 --> 00:07:35.080
Wait.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.125
Ryoma Echizen!

00:07:42.253 --> 00:07:43.880
Th-The water tower!

00:07:53.431 --> 00:07:54.349
Boy...

00:07:56.267 --> 00:07:58.353
Don't underestimate the world.

00:08:03.191 --> 00:08:05.819
When next we meet, I'll beat you.

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:08.279
Just you wait.

00:08:13.493 --> 00:08:14.661
Koshimae...

00:08:20.125 --> 00:08:22.127
Koshimae!

00:08:31.594 --> 00:08:34.055
This is the camp exit.

00:08:35.348 --> 00:08:37.475
Are you abandoning the camp?

00:08:38.018 --> 00:08:40.520
I don't have a reason to be here anymore.

00:08:41.104 --> 00:08:43.773
You think you'll get away with that?

00:08:44.065 --> 00:08:47.277
I don't care if you don't let me pass.

00:08:47.277 --> 00:08:49.654
I always do what I want.

00:09:06.504 --> 00:09:09.382
Oh, yeah. I should give this back.

00:09:12.302 --> 00:09:16.348
Give it to someone you think is worthy of it.

00:09:28.985 --> 00:09:30.195
You're awake?

00:09:31.071 --> 00:09:32.655
Um, I...

00:09:32.655 --> 00:09:33.698
It's over.

00:09:34.115 --> 00:09:37.702
The second string only won the first round.

00:09:38.161 --> 00:09:39.579
The first string crushed them.

00:09:40.914 --> 00:09:42.624
What about Ryoma Echizen?

00:09:42.624 --> 00:09:44.584
He left the camp.

00:09:47.337 --> 00:09:48.963
I'm sorry.

00:09:49.923 --> 00:09:52.509
You guys went through all that to train me,

00:09:52.967 --> 00:09:53.927
but I...

00:09:54.511 --> 00:09:56.513
And even Echizen...

00:09:56.513 --> 00:09:59.432
I'm excited for his future.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.017
Yeah.

00:10:01.434 --> 00:10:03.228
Same goes for yours, Tokugawa.

00:10:04.229 --> 00:10:06.940
Don't apologize. Just win the next one.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:10.235
And for now, just rest.

00:10:10.694 --> 00:10:12.195
You worked hard.

00:10:12.612 --> 00:10:13.780
Oni-<i>san</i>...

00:10:15.448 --> 00:10:16.700
Thanks.

00:10:19.494 --> 00:10:21.204
Huh? Oni...

00:10:21.204 --> 00:10:25.125
I thought men could only cry when
they achieved their greatest desire.

00:10:25.834 --> 00:10:29.045
Y-You idiot! This is sweat!

00:11:01.327 --> 00:11:02.579
Ryoma-kun?

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.585
Why are you here?
What about the training camp?

00:11:11.421 --> 00:11:12.505
Ryoma-<i>kun</i>!

00:11:15.383 --> 00:11:17.093
Okay, Ryuzaki,

00:11:17.093 --> 00:11:18.928
can you hang out for a bit?

00:12:02.055 --> 00:12:04.182
Hey! What are you kids doi--

00:12:04.933 --> 00:12:05.892
Ryuzaki!

00:12:07.686 --> 00:12:10.063
W-We're sorry!

00:12:18.947 --> 00:12:21.116
Ryoma-<i>kun</i>, is something wrong?

00:12:21.116 --> 00:12:23.493
You're acting weird today.

00:12:23.493 --> 00:12:24.577
Not really.

00:12:25.537 --> 00:12:27.330
And you? What were you doing?

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:30.750
I was going to Miura Shrine
to pray for victory.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.168
Victory?

00:12:33.753 --> 00:12:37.549
So you'd be chosen for
the Japanese team.

00:12:38.299 --> 00:12:42.095
A-And... I drew your fortune for you.

00:12:46.474 --> 00:12:48.685
Wait, that's...

00:12:49.102 --> 00:12:50.729
"Bad Luck"

00:12:50.729 --> 00:12:53.023
"Bad Luck"
So these really do exist.

00:12:53.023 --> 00:12:55.400
N-No! Not that one!

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:57.444
I drew a second one...

00:12:59.195 --> 00:13:01.614
Bad luck, bad luck, bad luck...

00:13:01.614 --> 00:13:03.950
And these are bad luck, bad luck, bad luck...

00:13:04.659 --> 00:13:06.911
No, no! Don't be so depressed!

00:13:07.328 --> 00:13:08.955
Doesn't bother me.

00:13:08.955 --> 00:13:09.706
Ryoma-<i>kun</i>!

00:13:13.335 --> 00:13:13.710
"Good Luck"

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:14.669
"Good Luck"
Here.

00:13:14.669 --> 00:13:16.087
"Good Luck"

00:13:17.589 --> 00:13:19.007
It's okay.

00:13:20.342 --> 00:13:23.345
I know something good
will come of it in the end.

00:13:27.265 --> 00:13:29.351
How much did you spend on these?

00:13:33.438 --> 00:13:35.190
See you later, Ryoma-<i>kun</i>.

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:35.940
Yeah.

00:13:38.318 --> 00:13:39.986
Hey, Ryuzaki.

00:13:41.988 --> 00:13:42.989
Thanks.

00:13:54.834 --> 00:13:57.545
Well? Aren't you getting in?

00:14:03.718 --> 00:14:05.595
How's Tokugawa?

00:14:05.595 --> 00:14:08.181
He managed to escape shortening his career.

00:14:08.181 --> 00:14:11.726
But I still don't like your methods.

00:14:12.394 --> 00:14:13.895
You haven't changed.

00:14:13.895 --> 00:14:16.940
That's why all of you are too soft.

00:14:17.273 --> 00:14:18.108
What?

00:14:22.112 --> 00:14:23.697
Koshimae...

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:27.617
Moping won't bring Echizen-kun back.

00:14:27.867 --> 00:14:29.744
Yeah, but, Shiraishi...

00:14:29.744 --> 00:14:32.330
Train hard here for his sake, too.

00:14:33.123 --> 00:14:36.376
That's all you can do, Kin-<i>chan</i>.

00:14:36.376 --> 00:14:37.168
Yeah...

00:14:38.878 --> 00:14:40.839
First Kabaji, now this...

00:14:40.839 --> 00:14:43.508
I refuse to accept this camp's methods!

00:14:43.758 --> 00:14:47.178
Kabaji and Echizen both left without a fuss.

00:14:47.178 --> 00:14:50.849
It'd be super lame for those
of us still here to complain.

00:14:50.849 --> 00:14:52.142
Shishido-<i>san</i>...

00:14:52.559 --> 00:14:55.562
They were prepared for the consequences.

00:14:59.566 --> 00:15:01.192
Bring back Koshimae!

00:15:01.192 --> 00:15:03.528
Your methods are awful!

00:15:03.528 --> 00:15:06.990
How could you attack Tokugawa-<i>san</i>
while he's injured?

00:15:11.244 --> 00:15:13.830
You can't conquer the world with honor alone.

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:15.749
That scar...

00:15:15.999 --> 00:15:19.169
Out there, the slightest mistake is fatal.

00:15:19.544 --> 00:15:23.089
One soft man can ruin an entire team.

00:15:24.632 --> 00:15:28.386
I will lead Japanese tennis
to the top of the world!

00:15:28.386 --> 00:15:31.181
And to get there, I will
not change my methods!

00:15:36.394 --> 00:15:39.147
Give that back to Tono later.

00:15:49.574 --> 00:15:51.201
Not yet...

00:15:51.576 --> 00:15:54.204
I'm not finished yet...

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:58.500
I don't need to be put out of my misery yet.

00:16:03.588 --> 00:16:04.631
That's the resolve

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:08.009
you need to take on the world...

00:16:20.563 --> 00:16:23.233
I was mistaken.

00:16:25.402 --> 00:16:28.905
I wasn't willing to die to beat you.

00:16:29.489 --> 00:16:32.534
I'm willing to die to surpass you...

00:16:34.327 --> 00:16:35.829
...and conquer the world.

00:16:36.788 --> 00:16:40.834
You're starting to look like
you've risen from the dead.

00:16:42.419 --> 00:16:47.173
You're the first man to appear
before me three times.

00:16:50.552 --> 00:16:52.053
That's not a compliment.

00:16:56.141 --> 00:16:58.852
I will show you true hell.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:20.540
Boy...

00:17:21.207 --> 00:17:23.376
Don't underestimate the world.

00:17:33.678 --> 00:17:35.388
You want to beat him?

00:17:37.307 --> 00:17:38.892
Hey, Shorty.

00:17:39.309 --> 00:17:40.769
What are you doing?

00:17:40.769 --> 00:17:42.270
The camp's still going on.

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:45.440
And someone I know can't go back there.

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:47.317
You want to beat him,

00:17:47.317 --> 00:17:49.861
but you have nowhere to fight.

00:17:50.236 --> 00:17:51.654
You're in the way.

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:57.077
The U-17 World Cup is coming up.

00:17:57.077 --> 00:17:58.453
World Cup?

00:17:59.162 --> 00:18:00.747
If you're in it,

00:18:00.747 --> 00:18:03.708
you'll have a chance to play against
him as he represents Japan.

00:18:05.043 --> 00:18:07.295
Fight with me there.

00:18:08.213 --> 00:18:10.548
Representing America.

00:18:13.343 --> 00:18:15.970
The U-17 World Cup?

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:21.559
Yeah. They've announced the 14
members of the Japanese team.

00:18:21.559 --> 00:18:22.977
"1. Houoh Byodoin" "2. Shuji Tanegashima"
"3. Duke Watanabe" "4. Kazuya Tokugawa"

00:18:22.977 --> 00:18:25.271
"1. Houoh Byodoin" "2. Shuji Tanegashima"
"3. Duke Watanabe" "4. Kazuya Tokugawa"
Tokugawa-<i>san</i>'s there.

00:18:25.271 --> 00:18:26.314
"1. Houoh Byodoin" "2. Shuji Tanegashima"
"3. Duke Watanabe" "4. Kazuya Tokugawa"

00:18:27.524 --> 00:18:28.775
That's...

00:18:28.775 --> 00:18:31.486
...the Cessna that rained
balls on us the first day.

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:36.449
What's going on?

00:18:37.409 --> 00:18:38.618
It's landing!

00:18:39.577 --> 00:18:42.330
The coach is finally here.

00:18:42.706 --> 00:18:43.873
The coach?

00:18:49.462 --> 00:18:52.132
It's been a while, trash.

00:18:52.549 --> 00:18:53.925
That voice...

00:18:55.260 --> 00:19:00.974
I'm the head coach of the U-17
Japanese team, Nyudo Mifune!

00:19:00.974 --> 00:19:04.185
Seriously? He's the coach?

00:19:05.437 --> 00:19:08.606
You guys know this dude?

00:19:09.691 --> 00:19:10.900
Listen up!

00:19:11.443 --> 00:19:15.363
To promote the growth of young players,

00:19:15.363 --> 00:19:19.159
the International Tennis Committee
is allowing middle school teams

00:19:19.159 --> 00:19:22.829
to participate in this year's U-17 World Cup!

00:19:22.829 --> 00:19:26.249
You mean we get to play
against the world, too?

00:19:26.791 --> 00:19:30.962
I have witnessed your mental
strength and potential!

00:19:31.296 --> 00:19:33.590
After speaking with your coaches,

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:37.218
I've chosen the middle school
representatives who will face the world!

00:19:37.552 --> 00:19:38.595
Representatives...

00:19:39.095 --> 00:19:42.932
This is why we invited middle schoolers

00:19:43.475 --> 00:19:46.353
from all over the nation to this camp!

00:19:47.979 --> 00:19:53.193
I will now announce the fourteen
middle school representatives!

00:20:00.575 --> 00:20:04.412
The thirteen U-17 Japanese
middle school representatives...

00:20:07.499 --> 00:20:11.503
have come to challenge Japan's
high school representatives.

00:20:12.921 --> 00:20:14.047
Very well.

00:20:14.464 --> 00:20:15.382
Come!

00:20:16.549 --> 00:20:20.804
U-17 World Cup Middle School
Japanese Representative Captain!

00:20:21.096 --> 00:20:22.597
Keigo Atobe!

00:20:22.597 --> 00:20:25.100
Captain? Of course.

00:20:26.601 --> 00:20:28.436
Seiichi Yukimura!

00:20:28.436 --> 00:20:29.938
A battle against the world...

00:20:30.313 --> 00:20:32.565
Let's get started!

00:20:33.191 --> 00:20:34.943
Kuranosuke Shiraishi!

00:20:34.943 --> 00:20:37.320
Ahh... Ecstasy!

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:39.155
Genichiroh Sanada!

00:20:39.155 --> 00:20:42.409
My resolve is solid as a rock!

00:20:43.243 --> 00:20:44.786
Jin Akutsu!

00:20:46.454 --> 00:20:48.289
Kintaro Toyama!

00:20:48.289 --> 00:20:50.792
I'm getting excited!

00:20:51.209 --> 00:20:52.794
Bunta Marui!

00:20:54.004 --> 00:20:55.422
Shusuke Fuji!

00:20:56.214 --> 00:20:57.924
Masaharu Niou!

00:20:58.258 --> 00:20:59.467
Gin Ishida!

00:21:00.885 --> 00:21:02.971
Shuichiroh Oishi!

00:21:03.972 --> 00:21:05.765
Eishiroh Kite!

00:21:05.765 --> 00:21:08.768
Let's show the world our strength.

00:21:10.395 --> 00:21:12.063
Akaya Kirihara!

00:21:12.063 --> 00:21:15.608
I'll climb to the world's greatest heights!

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:19.946
Prepare yourselves, boys.

00:21:21.781 --> 00:21:25.660
Top class champions from around the
world will gather at the World Cup.

00:21:27.454 --> 00:21:29.372
It's a battlefield.

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:33.168
And finally...

00:21:34.586 --> 00:21:36.629
Ryoma Echizen!

00:21:38.089 --> 00:21:40.508
The U-17 World Cup winner...

00:21:42.260 --> 00:23:18.443
...will be me.
